WEBVTT

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.070
Wow. So this is the Nanana's 
Collection treasure from that room?

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.070
All he did was add water, and it made tea!

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.920
Hence, "The Teapot That 
Requires No Leaves," huh?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.520
Its official name is "Xian Cha Fei."

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.010
Drinking this tea is a special 
privilege of the Adventure Club.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.350
I would like to formally welcome you 
all as new Adventure Club members.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.840
I'm so happy to have three new, 
highly-capable members joining us.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.970
May I ask one question?

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:48.740
Please.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.530
What exactly does this club do, anyway?

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.530
He didn't buy any...

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.160
I see. Nanana's Collection...

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:06.550
Yuiga-dono, it has been ten years 
since Ryuugajou Nanana died.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.960
But I believe Third High School 
was completed six years ago.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.760
That is correct.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.850
So who hid the Nanana's
 Collection treasure in this school?

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.260
I never expected you
 to ask me that so quickly.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.100
You certainly are a master detective.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.310
Oh, don't praise me so.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.270
But I don't know the answer to that.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.410
The one who hid the 
treasures of Nanana's Collection

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.740
is called the "Leprechaun."

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.450
And places where the treasures 
are hidden are called "ruins."

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.200
Even now, they continue to
 appear on Nanae Island all the time.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.270
By the way. I'm sorry to ask
 when you've just joined,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.080
but Yama-kun, I have a favor to ask you.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.790
What?

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.010
It's something that only you can do,
 as the resident of Room 202.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.990
Hey, Juugo...

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.230
"Ahh."

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.550
You really are useless!

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.280
How dare you feed me
 cheap three-for-98-yen pudding!

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.650
If you're a man, the least you can do

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:53.070
is buy your woman
 Randoya Light Pudding every day!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.870
You good-for-nothing loser!

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.610
Now that you've completed 
the "pretend lovers" trial,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.360
I'll give you a hint about
 finding the ruins, as promised.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.860
Within a tower rising high into the sky,

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.860
it rests inside a glass box.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.500
Let's do it again sometime.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.650
Next time, we'll act
 out something else.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.400
<b><u>Episode 3:</u></b>

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.400
The Ruins 1,000 Meters Above Ground

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.880
She put you through a trial like that?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.450
She made Konjou-senpai
 do all sorts of things, too.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:53.020
But why won't Nanana-chan
 just tell me where the ruins are?

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.260
Nanana-san has a unique way of thinking...

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.980
Her own set of rules, you might say.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.440
You could call them "Nanana's Rules."

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.070
When it comes to
 hunting for Nanana's Collection,

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.910
Nanana-san maintains a 
neutral stance at all times.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.410
Neutral?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.950
Yes. She doesn't tell
 anyone where the ruins are,

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.370
or how to solve the
 puzzles found within them.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.340
But she does provide as
 much information as is necessary.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.550
If you bring her a treasure
 you've found, she'll tell you about it.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.680
<i>I see...</i>

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.910
<i>So that's why she's even neutral toward me,</i>

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.020
<i>the one who's trying to 
help her find her killer...</i>

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.870
It was the same for Konjou-senpai.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.800
Nanana's Rules are
 absolutely unbreakable, huh?

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.670
Well, we're counting on you.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.800
Same to you.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.870
Um, who is Konjou-san?

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.820
A senpai two years older than me.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.500
Above all, she was very cheerful.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.460
She had guts, and she could take action.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.940
She was like an older sister.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.030
Oh...

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.770
She was smart, too.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.480
Her quick wit saved us 
from many a tight spot.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.960
<b>You have received a message.</b>

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.100
<b>Tensai
Found entrance to ruins on floor 164</b>

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.560
That was fast!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:21.980
<b>Shop Space for Rent
  First come, first serve!</b>

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.940
It's just a regular door. 
Why would it be here?

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.440
Could it just be a vacant shop space?

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.270
The doors like that on the other floors

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.960
required passcodes and key cards.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:36.700
But this one only has a passcode lock.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.670
Also, go to the room
 across from it. You'll see.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.740
Do you see it?

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.760
See what?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.470
We're looking at a hexagonal building, 
but there's a corner there.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.600
And the room in question is not vacant.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:58.560
Also, all the rooms appear 
horizontally flipped.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.980
That's pretty hard to notice...

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.920
It's a mirror trick.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.940
Now, where does the room
 with the ruins appear to be?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.830
There's no entrance.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:16.950
Looks like we hit the bullseye.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.140
Nicely done, Tensai-kun.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.420
So we know this door leads to the ruins.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.880
But, unfortunately,
 we don't know the passcode.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.250
Six digits?

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.620
As soon as we found out the
 ruins were in the Rising Building,

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.520
I did some research in advance.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.630
October 11th is the birthday of
 this building's architect, Mutsumi Koma.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:51.530
So, 6 from the "mutsu" in Mutsumi Koma, 
an asterisk, and then 1011?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.280
What made you think those 
numbers would be the passcode?

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:57.250
Nanana-san always thinks of her friends.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.620
I thought she might do that for 
the passcode to a building that

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.510
was so important to him.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.630
You're amazing, Isshin-sama!

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:08.960
Now, I think we should choose 
the members to go in from here.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.220
Choose members?

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.300
It's not necessarily best 
to go in large numbers.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.260
Unlike the test room,
 I've never seen these ruins before.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.930
We'll be risking our lives.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:29.020
The team will be myself, 
Yama-kun, and Tensai-kun.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:29.730
Agreed?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.040
Yuu, wait here with Daruku-kun,

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:36.650
and stand by in case anything happens to us.

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:38.160
Be safe.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.630
Be careful, Tensai.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.040
We're risking our lives, he says.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.460
Yeah. It'll be fine.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.280
We'll beat this with no problem.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.590
You're right.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.720
Well, shall we go, then?

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.470
Something's there!

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.300
Tensai!

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.250
Now, what was that all about...

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.480
The passage is back.

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.570
It's soft...

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.400
What do we do?

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.940
Let's try this way.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.670
<i>This is bad! This is bad! This is bad!</i>

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.090
<i>Tensai's gonna die!</i>

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.010
Juugo...

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:12.560
What?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.320
Thanks. You saved me.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.660
It was nothing. Remember, you owe me one.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.160
Yeah. I owe you one.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.580
I see. So that's the setup...

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.830
Juugo, you're up.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.410
Huh?

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:44.630
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.340
<i>You're gonna regret this if I die, Tensai!</i>

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.450
This spider moves in a set pattern.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.570
The passages collapse in 
two points at one time.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:08.250
Only one of those can 
be repaired at one time.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.750
If a human is there, it won't be repaired.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.880
And it takes about five minutes 
for a repaired passage to harden.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.130
Until then, that passage won't collapse.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:22.040
In other words, we just need to follow

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.750
a path made of newly-formed passages

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.880
from here to the
 location of the treasure chest.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:31.330
Soon, he'll complete
 the path I've drawn here.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.740
Yuiga-dono,
 the moment he completes the path,

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:35.860
you run for the treasure chest.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.730
Got it.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.360
Juugo! Take a left next!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.110
One more spot!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.570
Juugo! Left!

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.010
Now, Yuiga-dono!

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:32.560
Indeed! It was no match 
for this master detective.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.100
Could this really be...

00:13:58.530 --> 00:13:59.730
President Yuiga?

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.940
Don't move, both of you.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:17.040
What's going on?!

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.050
I've wanted this cane for so long!

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.670
Take me to the exit!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.100
Well, so long, you two.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.960
You can't be serious!

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.070
Ow, ow!

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:44.780
He's serious.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:53.620
You're all right?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.280
Um, where are the others?

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:05.300
Oh, I left them in there.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.050
But why?!

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:11.470
Daruku-kun, take a little nap.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.780
What do we do with her?

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:25.010
Leave her there. She can't do anything.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.640
No, Tensai...

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:27.930
More importantly, contact Ikkaku Shunjuu.

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:28.360
I said stop...

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:29.950
Tell him we got one of Nanana's Collection.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:31.320
Understood.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.250
Are you there, Kagetora?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.290
<i>Yes.</i>

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.750
The ruins crumbled and fell.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:43.330
How are things on the lower floors?

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.800
<i>Really? Nothing has changed here.</i>

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:50.150
I see. I'm glad no one was hurt.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.660
<i>Are you sure about this, Isshin?</i>

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.580
About what?

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.260
<i>About those two.</i>

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:59.030
They'll be fine.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.890
They're both much sharper 
and more skilled than I am.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.600
They'll make it out on their own.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:10.690
I seriously don't get this!
 It makes no sense!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.590
Ruins are pretty incredible...

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.980
No one can even see us.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:23.560
The treasure chest is
 surrounded by mirror-like surfaces.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:26.900
What are you doing?

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.880
Oh, I contacted the police, 
so help should be coming soon.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.510
We're just killing time until then.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:36.110
Juugo, your breath is tickling me.

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.640
Loosen up a little...

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.720
Watch it!

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:42.270
What?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.730
I don't really like this feeling.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.620
Huh?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:48.500
Hey!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.870
What are you trying to do?

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.780
Is this what they call the 
suspension bridge effect?

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.260
I came dangerously
 close to falling for you...

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.080
What are you so worked up about?

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:09.310
Sh-Shut up!
 I've never hugged a man before!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.580
And what about you?

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.050
Huh? What about me?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.560
I'm asking if you feel 
nothing when you have a

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.930
member of the opposite sex in your arms!

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:26.290
Are you getting worked up now, too?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.520
Shut up! You're in the 
same position, aren't you?

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.720
I-I just...

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:34.110
have high blood pressure.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.570
Then I just have high blood pressure, too.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:45.540
By the way, why are you a master detective?

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.930
To leave my name on history.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.630
That's not something you tell people.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.550
Why?

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:55.550
When you said it in the classroom, 
everyone laughed at you.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.510
I don't like being made fun of, 
but I won't stop saying it.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.970
Because I'd like not
 being able to say it even less.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.960
I know what people think about me.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.650
But I still want to
 become a master detective.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.360
You're a real idiot.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.050
And why is my useless assistant

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:32.580
sleeping without a care in the world?

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.800
That hurts...

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.550
Good morning, Daruku. 
Nice way to wake up, huh?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.340
Tensai!

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:48.250
Now, will you tell us 
what happened in detail?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:56.880
You don't intend to let him get 
away what what he did to us, right?

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.330
You better believe it.

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:01.200
I won't feel better until 
I deck that club president.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.770
I feel the same.

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:06.230
I won't be satisfied until 
I've taught him a lesson.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.780
So what do we do?

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.180
Let me leave.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.330
I think I know where 
Yuiga-dono may have gone.

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:14.290
Got it. Leave the rest to me.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:20.040
Excuse me, officers.
 Could you let these two go?

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.050
I'll tell you what happened myself.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.020
All right.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.720
Let's go, then.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:43.450
Now, why don't you tell me everything

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.450
you know about Nanana's Collection?

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.920
I-I'm home.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.390
Why do you look like that?

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.760
Well, see...

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:10.730
Okay, I get it. Put your clothes on.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:15.310
Nanana-chan, what was that cane?

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:17.270
The Wizard's Cane.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:20.530
It's officially called 
"Dovold Van Zamus's Cane."

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.930
It's a cane that was used by a
 real wizard in the Middle Ages,

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.740
but the cane itself holds 
great magical power, too.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:31.680
How did President Yuiga know about it?

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.180
I wonder...

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:39.880
Maybe it was one of the things I 
mentioned when I talked to him before.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.260
What? Are you that careless, Nanana-chan?

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.780
No, I'm not.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:49.260
So, what kind of power does that cane have?

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.950
The Wizard's Cane can

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:56.520
bring about anything its 
bearer wishes to happen.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:01.440
What the heck? It must be invincible, then!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.410
Actually, it's not.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:06.570
Huh? It's not?

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.400
<b>You have received a message.</b>

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:14.900
<b>Tensai 
President Yuiga will make a deal with the head of the Great 7, Ikkaku Shunjuu.</b>

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:54.340
I've been waiting for you, Juugo.
